rgins":-0.020817445609091045,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":29.2,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.12752330541115175,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.12554455445544555,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.03348,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":22.3,"_gate_insider_buying":0.25,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":25.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Coursera, Inc. operates an online learning platform that provides education and skills training in the United States, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, the Asia Pacific, and internationally. It operates through Consumer and Enterprise segments. The company offers guided projects, courses, and specializations; online bachelor's and master's degrees; postgraduate diplomas; and certificates for entry-level professional, non-entry level professional, university, and MasterTrack programs in the domains of business, computer science, technology, and data science through Coursera.org for Individuals, Coursera Plus, Coursera for Enterprise, Coursera for Business, Coursera for Campus, and Coursera for Government; Helix, AI-native platform connecting skills discovery and personalized learning to verified capability and business outcomes. It offers its products to individuals, businesses, institutions, employers, colleges and universities, organizations, and governments. The company was formerly known as Dkandu, Inc. and changed its name to Coursera, Inc. in April 2012. Coursera, Inc. was incorporated in 2011 and is headquartered in Mountain View, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Gregory M. Hart | CEO, President & Director | Age 55 | Compensation: $1.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $580K ranks in the above the sector median among Consumer Defensive peers, improving at 16%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $82K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $73K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Coursera, Inc. is a small-cap consumer defensive business with a $1.1B market cap on $758M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +13% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +6.1pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Gross margins of 55% are the starting point for assessing pricing power.","The business throws off $107M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 14 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","Accruals are elevated at -16.0% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 13% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 3.3% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 17% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 59% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.5894974037425296},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.8% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (75% sell ratio) over the past year","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.25},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Slow-motion taste and channel shifts \u2014 private label, Gen-Z health preferences, or a DTC disruption can erode decade-old brand moats without a single dramatic quarter.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 and health-trend demand destruction \u2014 weight-loss drugs and wellness shifts are structurally reducing consumption in snack, beverage, and packaged food categories.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Large open-market insider purchases (net $32.0M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Growing faster than most Consumer Defensive peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Consumer Defensive sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 11% over 3 months","Consumer Defensive ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Consumer Defensive tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Coursera (COUR): A Low Earnings Multiple Meets the Udemy Integration Test","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/coursera-cour-low-earnings-multiple-234009652.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794008409.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.765,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Coursera (NYSE:COUR) Major Shareholder Pale Fire Capital Se Purchases 2,526,702 Shares of Company Stock","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https